\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {The truck rattled down the coastal road, every stone and rut announcing itself through the frame. The suspension had long since given up, so each jolt went straight through the seats and into my bones. The coastline of Weshaven was beautiful if you weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t the one behind the wheel\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 steep hills, crashing sea below\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 but with gravel and mud sucking at the tires, beauty came second to survival.}
\par\plain {We entered the Deep Woods, where the canopy pressed so close overhead that daylight turned green. Branches clawed at the glass, and the smell of damp earth filled the cab. I eased around a pothole that looked shallow, then wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 tires sloshing through mud before catching gravel again.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you alright, Edward?\u8221\'94 Mother\u8217\'92s voice cut into the grinding of the engine.}
\par\plain {I blinked, realizing I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been staring at the road so hard I hadn\u8217\'92t even breathed. \u8220\'93What\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 um, fine. Yeah. I mean\u8230\'85 no, I\u8217\'92m not.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know you\u8217\'92ve got a history with Liese, Eddie.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {That caught me. Almost nobody called me Eddie anymore\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 just people my own age back when I still had friends there. From her, it felt personal, like she was pulling open an old wound.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I would\u8217\'92ve gone alone if I could,\u8221\'94 she continued, her voice softer now, \u8220\'93but you know\u8230\'85\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I get it, Mom,\u8221\'94 I said, forcing a smirk. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re getting older. You\u8217\'92d probably ram the car off the cliff if you drove it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {She laughed, sudden and bright, the kind of laugh I hadn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t heard since Father was alive. \u8220\'93You sound exactly like your father.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Her hand touched my arm, just briefly. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93An alchemist, just like your father.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I stayed silent, eyes locked on the road ahead. Mud. Gravel. Sharp turn. Anything but her words.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Just forgive them, Edward,\u8221\'94 she said at last. \u8220\'93If you were my age, you\u8217\'92d understand\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 there\u8217\'92s no use holding onto that.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I let out a dry chuckle. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well\u8230\'85 thank God I\u8217\'92m not your age, right?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Her smile lingered, faint and wistful, but she said no more. The truck rattled on, deeper into the woods.}
\par\plain {The quiet didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t last.}
\par\plain {Wham! The truck lurched downward with a violent jolt, throwing me against the wheel. The whole frame groaned like something had caught it from underneath.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Shit!\u8221\'94 I snapped, fumbling the gears.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What happened?!\u8221\'94 Mother\u8217\'92s hand gripped the dash, her eyes darting to the trees.}
\par\plain {I dropped it into first, pressed the gas\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 nothing but a muddy spin of the tires. Tried again, harder. Same result.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yeah\u8230\'85 seems like we\u8217\'92re stuck.\u8221\'94 I blew out a long breath, trying not to curse again.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Here?\u8221\'94 she asked, voice sharp with unease. The Deep Woods swallowed the word whole.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It should be no problem,\u8221\'94 I muttered, already reaching under the seat. My boots clattered against the floorboards as I pulled them on. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll get it unstuck. Can you give it gas when I tell you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {She nodded, lips tight. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Okay. Be safe.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I shoved the door open. Damp air rushed in, thick with loam and pine. The forest was silent in that particular way that wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t silence at all\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 bird calls cutting short, a rustle of brush where no wind moved, a crack somewhere deep between the trunks.}
\par\plain {The mud sucked at my boots as I sloshed around to the back wheels. My hands braced against the truck\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s frame, slick with wet earth. \u8220\'93Alright, gas it!\u8221\'94 I shouted.}
\par\plain {The engine growled, the tires spun, mud flinging across my jacket. But\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85}
\par\plain {Weird.}
\par\plain {The wheels weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t buried at all\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 clear as day, barely sunk into the road. They spun and spun, but the truck didn\u8217\'92t budge an inch.}
\par\plain {It wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t stuck.}
\par\plain {So why wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t it moving?}
\par\plain {I leaned down again, running my hand along the wheel. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright, gas it one more time, Mom!\u8221\'94 I called.}
\par\plain {The engine roared, the tires spun\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and my stomach sank.}
\par\plain {They weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t touching the ground anymore.}
\par\plain {The whole back end of the truck was floating, a good inch above the mud.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hello, friend.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The voice came from behind me.}
\par\plain {I spun around, nearly losing my footing in the muck. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What do you want?\u8221\'94 I barked, louder than I meant to.}
\par\plain {A man stood between the trees. Chestplate, helmet, a halberd taller than he was. The steel was nicked and dented, his breastplate smeared with blood\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not red, but something bluish. His beard was fire-red, a sharp goatee that matched the smirk tugging at his mouth.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Edward?\u8221\'94 my mother called from the cab, her voice sharp with concern. \u8220\'93Are you okay back there?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The man grinned wider. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Your mother can\u8217\'92t see us.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {My heart skipped.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I want a ride,\u8221\'94 he said easily, as if we were neighbors bartering over eggs. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re bound for Weshaven, I presume? My merry little friends and I are stuck in this cursed forest, collecting bounties. It\u8217\'92d be mighty helpful if you\u8217\'92d give us a lift back to town.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t trust you,\u8221\'94 I said flatly.}
\par\plain {The air hung heavy. He just stood there, staring at me through the slits of his helmet, and for a long moment the forest seemed to hold its breath.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Edward!\u8221\'94 Mother\u8217\'92s voice rang out again. I glanced back just as she threw open her cloak. Her wand flashed in her hand\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }
\par\plain {A streak of white light shot past me, aimed straight at his chest.}
\par\plain {Crack! It froze mid-air, splintering like glass against nothing.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She\u8217\'92s a damn witch,\u8221\'94 a voice spat.}
\par\plain {A girl stepped from the shadows, indigo hood pulled low, staff clutched in both hands. Its crystal glowed, pulsed\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and with a sudden shimmer, the truck settled back onto the road.}
\par\plain {My fists clenched. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who the fuck are you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The forest answered. More figures emerged from between the pines\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 two men with flintlocks leveled at me, another girl draped in furs with cold eyes that studied every move I made.}
\par\plain {Finally, the armored man took a step forward, his boots squelching in the mud. He tapped the butt of his halberd against the ground, casual as anything, though his grin never faltered.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m Fredrick,\u8221\'94 he said. He gestured with his chin to the others. \u8220\'93Rika the Huntress. Clover the Mage. Owen and Rowan, the sharpshooters. We\u8217\'92re Hunters out of King\u8217\'92s Grave. We collect bounties for slain monsters.\u8221\'94 }}